From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 03:30:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] avfilter/vf_hqdn3d_vulkan: add a Vulkan hqdn3d filter

Add hqdn3d_vulkan, the hqdn3d denoiser in two compute shaders: a
horizontal pass for the spatial line filter and a vertical pass for the
spatial column filter and the temporal filter. It runs the same integer
lookup tables as the CPU filter, which now come from hqdn3d_coefs.c so
that both filters share one implementation, and it takes the same
options and commands.

The output is bit-exact to hqdn3d for the planar 8, 10, 12 and 16 bit
formats and for nv12, p010, p012 and p016. The one exception: where the
CPU filter writes a value above the format maximum into a 10 or 12 bit
plane, p010 and p012 cannot store it, and this filter writes the format
maximum instead.

The temporal state is dropped where hqdn3d drops it: on graph
configuration and on a change of frame size or format within the
stream. After such a change the output frames come from a frames
context of the new size, so libavfilter users that send frames of a new
size into a running graph get output of that size, as with hqdn3d.

tools/hqdn3d_reset_test runs hqdn3d and hqdn3d_vulkan side by side on
frames of three sizes and compares every output frame.

The filter ports GPL code and therefore depends on --enable-gpl, as
hqdn3d does.

Signed-off-by: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
